# Cloudflare Pages header rules for the static export in `out/`.
#
# Root cause of the /tools ChunkLoadError: this repo had no `_headers` file, so
# Cloudflare Pages served every response (HTML *and* the content-hashed JS under
# /_next/static/) with its own default/heuristic caching instead of an explicit
# policy. That let an HTML page (or its RSC payload, e.g. tools.txt) be served
# stale from cache — still pointing at a chunk filename hash from a previous
# build — after that specific chunk file had already been superseded by a newer
# hash in a later deployment. The HTML said `page-49ee441999736ae7.js`; the live
# chunks directory only had that build's actual output, so the request 404'd and
# React's dynamic `import()` for the /tools route surfaced it as ChunkLoadError.
#
# Every file under /_next/static/ is content-hashed by webpack — a given hash
# never changes meaning, so it is always safe to cache immutably forever. HTML
# (and the paired .txt RSC payloads) must never be cached beyond revalidation,
# since they are the only thing that references those hashes by name.

/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
